    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will keep on delivering more chips every year, \nand that is this power limitation. According to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 566080,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "industry analysis, the biggest bottleneck facing \nnew data centers today is not necessarily in the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571040,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "advanced computer chips to run their models, but \nrather in getting the electrical infrastructure  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575200,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to support it. Power has become the realworld \nconstraint. So that's how these projects are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580400,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "getting compared in the same way we might compare \nFPS in Cyberpunk 2077. In a typical data center,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 586320,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the transformers, power supplies, generators, and \nconnecting wires typically take up less than 10%  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591520,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the total build cost. But nothing can happen \nuntil those components are in place. The price  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 597600,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of things like a Prolle transformer have more \nthan doubled over the last 4 years and supply  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602320,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "struggles to keep up with this new demand on top \nof supplying regular energy grids for regular  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606800,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "households and businesses. It hasn't helped that \na lot of these technical components have typically  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 611760,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "come from China, South Korea, Mexico, and Canada, \nmaking tariff disruptions harder to navigate.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 617440,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What this has meant is that since the supply of \neverything that goes into these data centers has  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 621680,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "been so limited, companies are buying everything \nthey can as soon as they can, even if it takes a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627040,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "long time to actually be put into use. If Nvidia \nsays the latest batch of HB200's is ready to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 632960,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "purchase, these companies are compelled to buy \nthem even if they don't actually have space to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637200,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "put them yet. Because if they don't, then they \nwill have to go to the back of the line again.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641760,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The same goes for other components like cooling or \nenergy supplies. Even if they don't have anywhere  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646400,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to use them right now, they are motivated to \nbuy them just in case. In industrial planning,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 651440,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is called the bullwhip effect. And it can \nhelp to explain the extreme levels of spending  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 655680,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the same time as very few projects seem to be \nmaking much progress. Now, this is a widespread  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 661040,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "issue across the world. But to really highlight \nthis problem, there are actually two new fully fit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 666560,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out data centers just up the road from Nvidia's \nheadquarters in Santa Clara that are sitting  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670960,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "completely offline because they are waiting for \nlocal utilities to catch up. At the moment, Nvidia  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 676160,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is benefiting greatly from this. They can almost \nguarantee that as soon as they get their chips  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680560,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from TSMC, they can immediately sell them off \nagain because there will be a buyer ready for it,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 685440,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even if it does end up sitting in a warehouse \nfor a few months. It's a dangerous game that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690240,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only takes a small demand correction to cause a \nmassive overupp. But for now, it's been incredibly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695680,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lucrative. Except that that assumption is starting \nto strain now. Nvidia ended its financial year in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702000,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "January, and when their annual reporting was \nreleased, they had again had a record year  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 706400,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in terms of sales in the top line and profit in \nthe bottom line. But some other numbers started  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 711200,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to catch people's eyes. primarily that their \ninventory had more than doubled from the year  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 715840,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before and quadrupled from 2024. If Nvidia \nreally is struggling to keep up with demand,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721520,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there really shouldn't be any reason why they \nare sitting on so much of their own product. This  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 725840,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is either suggesting that it's getting harder to \nmove these chips or more realistically that Nvidia  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730560,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "themselves are struggling with the same supply \nchain problems upstream of them and they are just  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 735520,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trying to get as much supply as possible with the \nconfidence that they will eventually be able to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739760,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sell it to someone. Ironically, when this anomaly \nwas initially highlighted, it was actually an LLM  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 745200,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "market algorithm that found the disconnect first \nalongside the trend of their customers taking a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 749760,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "longer time to actually pay for their receivables. \nSo, yeah, the power issue was already a major  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 755520,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "problem. But today, there is also the energy issue \non top of that. When these facilities are fully  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761120,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "operational, they draw a lot of power. And power \nover time is energy. And energy has already become  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 767440,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "very expensive over the last few years thanks \nlargely to these very same data centers. But  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772400,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the war in Iran has well I would say poured fuel \non the fire. But it's kind of done the opposite  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 779040,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of that. Higher energy prices significantly cut \ninto the viability of running these centers and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784000,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the cash burn rates associated with them. So far, \nmost data centers get their energy directly from  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 788880,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the local energy grid, which means now they are \ngoing to be paying more money and waiting even  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 793680,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "longer for capacity to come online. Other newer \ncenters have gotten around this by using their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 798320,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "own natural gas turbine generators. But well, \nnatural gas has just doubled in price, doubling  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804320,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the largest line item in their ongoing expenses. \nIt's not great, but it all gets much worse when  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809760,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you consider these issues in the context of the \nthird major problem facing Nvidia right now,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814480,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that is how long these chips are expected \nto last. Now, not to yank my own crank here,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819440,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but about 8 months ago in our video on Amazon's \nAI spending, we highlighted the problem of capital  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824080,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "expenditure going towards cuttingedge chips, \nwhich by their nature depreciate extremely  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828720,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quickly as newer, better models come out. Well, \n4 months later, Michael Bur of Big Short Fame,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 834400,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as well as a handful of other investors, put \nout pieces effectively saying the same thing.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 839120,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The industry standard amongst the big tech \ncompanies is to depreciate these GPUs over 6  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 843280,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "years when in reality they would be lucky to \nstay operationally viable for 3 years. This  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 848400,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just basically means that they count 16 of the \npurchase price against income to offset taxes,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 853200,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but also more accurately report the true annual \nprofitability of the business. By stretching  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 857840,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out depreciation for longer than reasonable, \nservice life of these cards makes expenses  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 861920,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "look better than they really should be for the \ncompanies that make up a majority of Nvidia's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 865840,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "demand. In a somewhat confusing rebuttal, Nvidia \nthemselves actually responded to this criticism  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870960,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by defending their own accounting practices, which \nwasn't the accusation in the first place. Nvidia  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 876960,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doesn't actually have that many hard assets at \nall. It is just a chip designer with most of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 881520,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the real hardware being manufactured by their \nsuppliers, primarily TSMC. So nobody really  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 886560,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cared about their depreciation schedules. \nThe point was if companies like Microsoft,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 891360,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oracle, and Meta had more honest accounting, it \nwould make their profits look worse, which may  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 896240,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reduce investor hype around AI investment and \nultimately the demand these companies have for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 900800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even more GPUs coming down the pipe. The reason \nthis critique was leveled at Nvidia specifically  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 905840,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is because if Microsoft is pressured into \nre-evaluating this accounting standard,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 909840,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they might lose a little bit of profitability \non paper, but they still have a major business  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 914320,
    "dDurationMs": 7920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outside of this AI stuff. But if they order fewer \nGPUs, well, that is Nvidia's entire business. Now,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 922240,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "both the ongoing supply bottlenecks and higher \nenergy prices make this problem much worse. If  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 927280,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nvidia is consistently releasing a new model of \nflagship AI GPUs every year that make everything  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 932480,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's come before it obsolete, then it could \nbecome much harder to justify purchasing pallets  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 936960,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of current-day chips in advance in the hope that \nthey will be ready when a data center eventually  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 940880,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "comes online because by that time they might \nalready be irrelevant. On the other end of the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 946320,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spectrum, the depreciation of chips already in \nservice becomes worse the higher energy prices  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 950880,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get. If energy prices are very low, it can remain \nworth it to run older, less efficient hardware,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 956080,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even if it uses much more energy to achieve the \nsame thing. But as energy prices have increased,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 960960,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those margins can be squeezed to the point where \nit costs more to run a server in energy inputs  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 965600,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "alone, than it could be rented out for. At that \npoint, multi-million dollar racks of last year's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970320,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cuttingedge hardware effectively become e-waste. \nNow, the market can stay irrational longer than  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 975680,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "any naysayers can stay solvent. And it is worth \nrealizing that even if the business case makes  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 980480,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no sense, it can stay in motion for as long \nas investors are happy to put money into it.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 984960,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But well, even that might be starting to change. \nFor the last four years, private credit companies  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 990240,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like Blue Owl and Black Rockck's Credit Arm \nhave been major financing partners on some of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 993920,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the biggest data center projects, but they are \nnow facing their own industry-wide problems,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 998160,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is going to make it much harder for \nthem to maintain the supply of easy financing.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1002320,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Go and watch this video next to find out what \nprivate credit actually is and why it has all  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1006640,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gone so badly wrong. And don't forget to like and \nsubscribe to keep on learning how money works."
    } ]
  } ]
